  "challenge": "ESCALATE is unnecessary: the packet already supports a clean REJECT. VN-001's own policy states unknown vendor is the entry point for most fraud, and the vendor tool returned no exact match and only below-threshold noise—no real candidate to hand procurement. Combined with zero invoice history, two IN-001 unknown SKUs (nothing to fulfill, no price check possible), an unverifiable billing@noproduct.biz domain, and a PO-002 near-threshold total that the policy explicitly flags as a structuring signature, there is no missing fact a human would retrieve that changes the picture. Onboarding a brand-new supplier and standing up two catalog SKUs is a procurement process, not an invoice exception; the submitted invoice fails every master-data gate and should be rejected as unsolicited rather than parked for confirmation.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["VN-001", "IN-001", "PO-002", "VN-003", "PR-004"]
}
